      "quiz_35_7_q": "What is sublimation?",
      "quiz_35_8_fb1": "Removing trees reduces the total leaf area, which decreases transpiration and makes the local climate drier.",
      "quiz_35_8_fb3": "Fewer trees mean less moisture is pumped into the air, leading to fewer clouds and less local rainfall.",
      "quiz_35_8_fb4": "Trees are key hydrologic pumps. Removing them severely disrupts local water cycles and increases flooding.",
      "quiz_35_8_opt1": "Increases evaporation",
      "quiz_35_8_opt2": "Reduces transpiration and increases runoff",
      "quiz_35_8_opt3": "Creates more clouds",
      "quiz_35_8_opt4": "Has no effect",
      "quiz_35_8_q": "How does deforestation affect the water cycle?",
      "quiz_68_1_fb1": "Wind enhances the evaporation rate by removing the boundary layer of moist air, but solar radiation is the thermodynamic driver.",
      "quiz_68_1_fb3": "Gravity is a downward force driving infiltration and precipitation, whereas solar energy drives water upward.",
      "quiz_68_1_fb4": "The Moon drives tides but does not supply the heat energy required for the latent heat of vaporization.",
