      "quiz_68_4_opt2": "Water release from plants",
      "quiz_68_4_opt3": "Snow melting",
      "quiz_68_4_opt4": "Rivers flowing",
      "quiz_68_4_q": "What is transpiration?",
      "quiz_68_5_fb2": "Freshwater is much scarcer! Only 3% is fresh, and about 68% of that is locked in glaciers and ice sheets.",
      "quiz_68_5_fb3": "Over 97% of Earth's water is salty ocean water. Fresh water is a tiny portion.",
      "quiz_68_5_fb4": "Half of Earth's water is saline. Freshwater is a scarce resource.",
      "quiz_68_5_opt1": "3%",
      "quiz_68_5_opt2": "10%",
      "quiz_68_5_opt3": "25%",
      "quiz_68_5_opt4": "50%",
      "quiz_68_5_q": "How much of Earth's water is freshwater?",
      "quiz_68_6_fb1": "Clouds are made of condensed vapor. Stomata are microscopic pores in plant epidermal layers.",
      "quiz_68_6_fb3": "Subsurface channels are aquifers. Stomata are biological valves regulating leaf transpiration.",
      "quiz_68_6_fb4": "Rain droplets are precipitation. Stomata are microscopic openings on leaves.",
