      "quiz_912_2_opt2": "Boyle's Law",
      "quiz_912_2_opt3": "Ohm's Law",
      "quiz_912_2_opt4": "Bernoulli's Principle",
      "quiz_912_2_q": "What law governs groundwater flow through saturated porous media?",
      "quiz_912_3_fb1": "This value is too low. Water requires about 2.45 megajoules per kilogram to vaporize.",
      "quiz_912_3_fb3": "This is the specific heat capacity of liquid water, not its latent heat of vaporization.",
      "quiz_912_3_fb4": "This is close to the latent heat of fusion (melting ice) which is 0.334 MJ/kg.",
      "quiz_912_3_opt1": "~1.0 MJ/kg",
      "quiz_912_3_opt2": "~2.45 MJ/kg",
      "quiz_912_3_opt3": "~4.18 MJ/kg",
      "quiz_912_3_opt4": "~0.33 MJ/kg",
      "quiz_912_3_q": "What is the latent heat of vaporization of water at 20°C?",
      "quiz_912_4_fb1": "This is too low. Saturation vapor pressure increases by approximately 7% per degree of heating.",
      "quiz_912_4_fb3": "This is too high. The capacity grows exponentially but is about 7% per degree Celsius.",
      "quiz_912_4_fb4": "This is too high. A 1 degree Celsius increase corresponds to a 7% capacity expansion.",
      "quiz_912_4_opt1": "~2%",
      "quiz_912_4_opt2": "~7%",
      "quiz_912_4_opt3": "~15%",
      "quiz_912_4_opt4": "~25%",
      "quiz_912_4_q": "The Clausius-Clapeyron relation predicts saturation vapor pressure increases by what per °C?",
      "quiz_912_5_fb1": "Navier-Stokes equations model momentum in open fluid dynamics, not unsaturated flow in soils.",
      "quiz_912_5_fb3": "Bernoulli's equation relates pressure and speed in open inviscid flows.",
      "quiz_912_5_fb4": "Poiseuille's equation describes flow through open cylindrical pipes.",
      "quiz_912_5_opt1": "Navier-Stokes",
      "quiz_912_5_opt2": "Richards' equation",
      "quiz_912_5_opt3": "Bernoulli's equation",
      "quiz_912_5_opt4": "Poiseuille's equation",
      "quiz_912_5_q": "What equation extends Darcy's Law to unsaturated flow?",
      "quiz_912_6_fb1": "This is too low. Average global cloud albedo is significant, reflecting about 30% of incoming light.",
      "quiz_912_6_fb3": "While specific storm clouds can be highly reflective, the global average is around 30%.",
      "quiz_912_6_fb4": "Only the densest storm clouds reflect 90%, whereas the global average is much lower.",
      "quiz_912_6_opt1": "Reflects ~5%",
      "quiz_912_6_opt2": "Reflects ~30%",
      "quiz_912_6_opt3": "Reflects ~60%",
      "quiz_912_6_opt4": "Reflects ~90%",
      "quiz_912_6_q": "What is cloud albedo's approximate effect on solar radiation?",
      "quiz_912_7_fb1": "This is the atmospheric residence time before precipitation, not the ocean residence time.",
      "quiz_912_7_fb2": "This is too short. Due to ocean volume, the average water molecule remains there for about 3,200 years.",
      "quiz_912_7_fb4": "This is too long. Oceanic circulation and evaporation cycle molecules much faster.",
      "quiz_912_7_opt1": "~9 days",
      "quiz_912_7_opt2": "~100 years",
      "quiz_912_7_opt3": "~3,200 years",
      "quiz_912_7_opt4": "~1 million years",
      "quiz_912_7_q": "What is the average residence time of a water molecule in the ocean?",
      "quiz_912_8_fb2": "This is a hydrological partition ratio, not the thermodynamic Bowen ratio.",
      "quiz_912_8_fb3": "This is a global water budget balance, not the Bowen ratio.",
      "quiz_912_8_fb4": "This relates to cloud cover fraction, not the Bowen heat flux ratio.",
      "quiz_912_8_opt1": "Ratio of sensible to latent heat flux",
