      "feathers": "Nsala",
      "dozens_of_dinosaurs_are_preserved_with": "Ba-dinosaurs ebele babombami na nsala, kobanda na nsala ya pɛtɛɛ tii na nsala ya solo ya kopumbwa. Mingi bazalaki na nsala kala liboso ete moko na bango akoka kopumbwa.",
      "the_wishbone": "Mokuwa ya mposa (furcula)",
      "birds_have_a_furcula_or_wishbone_so_di": "Bandeke bazali na furcula, to mokuwa ya mposa. Ba-dinosaurs ya theropod lokola T. rex na Velociraptor mpe bazalaki na yango. Ezali mokuwa kaka moko mpenza.",
      "hollow_air_filled_bones": "Mikuwa ya libulu oyo etondi na mopɛpɛ",
      "bird_bones_are_light_and_filled_with_a": "Mikuwa ya bandeke ezali pɛpɛlɛ mpe etondi na basaki ya mopɛpɛ. Mikuwa kaka wana oyo etondi na mopɛpɛ ebimaka na ba-dinosaurs mingi, eteni ya mosala ya kopema oyo ekokani na ndeke.",
      "three_toed_feet": "Makolo ya misapi misato",
      "the_classic_bird_footprint_three_toes_": "Litɔnɔ ya lokolo ya ndeke ya kala, misapi misato liboso, ekokani na makolo ya theropod. Bilembo ya lokolo ya fosile ya dinosaur emonanaka lokola bilembo ya lokolo ya bandeke minene.",
      "eggs_and_brooding": "Maki na kovanda likoló",
      "dinosaurs_laid_eggs_in_nests_and_some_": "Ba-dinosaurs ezalaki kobeta maki na bazala mpe mosusu, lokola Citipati na Oviraptor, ezalaki kovanda likoló na yango mpo na koyangela bana na yango, kaka ndenge bandeke esalaka.",
      "a_wrist_that_folds": "Lokuwa ya lobɔkɔ oyo egumbamaka",
      "birds_fold_their_wings_using_a_special": "Bandeke egumbaka mapapu na bango na nzela ya mokuwa ya lobɔkɔ ya sipesiale oyo ezali na lolenge ya sanza-ndambo. Mokuwa kaka wana epesaki ba-dinosaurs mosusu nzela ya kobenda mabɔkɔ na bango pene na nzoto.",
      "fast_growth_warm_bodies": "Bokoli ya mbangu, banzoto ya molunge",
      "growth_rings_in_dinosaur_bones_show_ma": "Ba-anɔ ya bokoli na mikuwa ya dinosaur emonisaka ete mingi ekólaki mbangu mpe ezalaki na makila ya molunge, lokola bandeke na banyama ya mabɛlɛ koleka banyama ya kokɔlɔma ya mikolo oyo.",
      "best_preserved_detail": "A baby with preserved internal organs, down to the intestines.",
      "biggest_bite_detail": "A bite force estimated near 35,000 newtons, the strongest of any known land animal.",
      "biggest_brain_detail": "Some of the highest brain-to-body ratios among dinosaurs.",
      "biggest_claw_detail": "Hand claws up to about a meter long, the longest of any known animal.",
      "biggest_hadrosaur_detail": "A crestless hadrosaur up to about 15 meters long.",
      "dinopark_note": "One of the richest dinosaur fossil areas in the world.",
      "djadochta_note": "An ancient desert that froze behavior in time, including the Fighting Dinosaurs.",
      "ext_devonian_note": "A drawn-out crisis rather than a single sudden blow.",
      "ext_kpg_note": "The only mass extinction firmly tied to an asteroid impact. Birds carry the dinosaur line forward.",
      "ext_ordovician_note": "The second-largest extinction, long before any land vertebrates walked.",
      "ext_permian_note": "About 19 of every 20 marine species disappeared. Recovery took millions of years.",
      "ext_triassic_note": "A case where extinction helped, not hurt, the dinosaurs.",
      "field_station_3d": "Field Station",
      "first_color_detail": "The first dinosaur whose color, a ginger-and-white tail, was worked out from fossils.",
      "first_named_detail": "Named in 1824, before the word \"dinosaur\" was coined in 1842.",
      "heaviest_detail": "A titanosaur estimated near 70 tonnes or more, among the largest land animals ever.",
      "hellcreek_note": "A window onto the very last days of the non-bird dinosaurs, right up to the K-Pg layer.",
      "ischigualasto_note": "The \"Valley of the Moon\", recording the dawn of the dinosaurs.",
      "kaiparowits_note": "A remote site revealing the lost southern world of the continent Laramidia.",
      "kemkem_note": "A river system that somehow supported several giant predators at once.",
      "longest_detail": "A diplodocid that may have stretched past 30 meters from nose to tail.",
      "longest_neck_detail": "Some neck estimates reach about 15 meters, the longest of any animal.",
      "longest_pred_detail": "About 15 meters long, the longest known meat-eating dinosaur.",
      "morrison_note": "The classic American \"dinosaur graveyard\" of the Jurassic giants.",
      "nemegt_note": "A river-and-floodplain world that preserved many strange Asian dinosaurs.",
      "smallest_detail": "Crow-sized four-winged gliders, among the smallest non-bird dinosaurs.",
      "solnhofen_note": "A still lagoon whose fine limestone preserved feathers in stunning detail.",
      "tendaguru_note": "An African match to the Morrison, excavated in huge early expeditions.",
      "twomedicine_note": "Egg Mountain here proved dinosaurs nested in colonies and cared for young.",
      "yixian_note": "Fine volcanic ash preserved feathers and even color. It transformed how we see dinosaurs."
