      "the_aws_cwi_exam": "📝 The AWS CWI Exam",
      "the_bright_dome_above_the_plate_is_the": "The bright dome above the plate is the ",
      "the_certified_welding_inspector_cwi_is": "The Certified Welding Inspector (CWI) is the gatekeeper. ~$70-110K pay, $1,150 exam, 3 parts (fundamentals, code book, hands-on). Visual inspection (VT), 5 NDT methods (PT, MT, UT, RT, ET), code interpretation, ethical responsibilities. Top of the welding career ladder for someone who reads + writes well.",
      "the_certified_welding_inspector_cwi_is_2": "The Certified Welding Inspector (CWI) is the gatekeeper between a finished weld and the customer who accepts it. CWIs apply codes (AWS D1.1, ASME, API) to determine acceptance + rejection of welds, oversee non-destructive testing, audit welder qualifications, and sign off on completed work. Often the only path to certify a fabrication shop's output.",
      "the_chronic_risks_will_affect_career_l": "⚠ The chronic risks (will affect career-long welders)",
      "the_cross_section_view_is_what_an_insp": "The cross-section view is what an inspector sees when they cut the weld in half + polish + etch with nital (carbon steel) or oxalic (stainless). ",
      "the_cwi_exam": "📝 The CWI exam",
      "the_cwi_exam_is_one_of_the_more_demand": "The CWI exam is one of the more demanding professional certifications in welding. Three parts, each 2 hours, given over 9 hours one day:",
