      "girdling_body": "Phloem sits just inside the bark; xylem is deeper in the wood. Remove a complete ring of bark and the leaves keep receiving water, so the tree looks fine for a whole season. But no sugar can reach the roots. The roots starve first, and only then does the top die.",
